WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.700
Do lash extensions ruin your natural lashes? The answer is all in the technique!

2
00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:11.414
Let's compare a correct bond 1 mm from the lid with sloppy, clumped glue.

3
00:00:11.414 --> 00:00:18.129
Done correctly: each extension sits on one natural lash, about 1 mm from the eyelid.

4
00:00:18.129 --> 00:00:24.981
No glue touches the skin, every lash stays separate, and your lashes grow and shed naturally.

5
00:00:24.981 --> 00:00:30.348
Done wrong: the glue clumps, sticking several lashes together or onto the skin.

6
00:00:30.348 --> 00:00:36.008
When one lash sheds, it pulls the neighbouring ones out too, and your lashes thin out.

7
00:00:36.008 --> 00:00:40.836
Extensions must suit your natural lashes: not too long and not too thick.

8
00:00:40.836 --> 00:00:46.263
A fine natural lash can't carry a heavy extension, and it breaks easily.

9
00:00:46.263 --> 00:00:50.078
When you want your extensions off, never pull them out yourself.

10
00:00:50.078 --> 00:00:55.504
At the salon they're removed with a glue remover, and your natural lashes stay intact.

11
00:00:55.504 --> 00:01:04.041
In short: correct technique, the right weight and safe removal keep your natural lashes healthy; only clumped glue damages them.

12
00:01:04.041 --> 00:01:08.345
